    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0838" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1531/95: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Keena</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-02T11:00:00-04:00">August 2, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. Your telegram No. 37, July 29, 6 p.m. The Department agrees with you that
                    time may be saved if this Government now submits a tentative final draft of the
                    agreement and this is accordingly being prepared. It will be sent you by air
                    mail as soon as it is completed.</p>
                <p>The telegraphic reply prepared to your 36, July 22, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d743-f1"/> will not be sent. The suggestions embodied therein as
                    well as in section <pb facs="0839" n="746" xml:id="pg746"/> 1 of your 37, July
                    29, 6 p.m., will be incorporated in the tentative draft.</p>
                <p>We assume you do not intend to present separately the changes in the general
                    provisions outlined in instruction 712 of July 20<anchor n="25" xml:id="d743-f2"
                    /> but will take them up with the Honduran Government en bloc together with the
                    other points on which agreement has not been reached when the final draft
                    reaches you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
